    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "The number of times the hour hand and the minute hand of a clock form a right angle with each other between 06:00 and 12:00 on the same day is",
    "image": "qimages/samf/junior-2000-r1/q08.webp",
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "12"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "11"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "10"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "6"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "5"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "B",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Relative speed",
        "body": "The minute hand gains $360-30=330^\\circ$ per hour on the hour hand, i.e. $5.5^\\circ$ per minute. They form a right angle whenever the gap is $90^\\circ+180^\\circ k$. After 12:00 this happens at $t=\\frac{90+180k}{5.5}$ minutes. For $360\\le t\\le720$ we need $1980\\le90+180k\\le3960$, i.e. $k=11,12,\\dots,21$: 11 times.\n\n**Answer: (B) 11**"
      },
      {
        "title": "List the times",
        "body": "Using the same formula, the right angles occur at about 6:16, 6:49, 7:22, 7:55, 8:27, 9:00, 9:33, 10:05, 10:38, 11:11 and 11:44. That is 11 times.\n\n**Answer: (B) 11**"
      }
    ],
    "topics": [
      "time-calendar",
      "rates"
    ],
    "difficulty": 3,
    "duplicateOf": null,
    "reviewNote": null
  },
