    "prompt": "Two ants start at point $A$ and walk at the same pace. One ant walks around a 3 cm by 3 cm square whilst the other walks around a 6 cm by 3 cm rectangle. What is the minimum distance, in centimetres, any one must cover before they meet again?",
    "image": "qimages/samf/junior-2000-r1/q12.webp",
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "18"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "72"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "216"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "36"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "108"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "D",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Lowest common multiple",
        "body": "One lap is 12 cm and the other 18 cm. The ants walk equal distances, and are together again at $A$ only when both have completed whole laps: the least common multiple $\\operatorname{lcm}(12,18)=36$ cm. (They cannot meet earlier: they share only the point A.)\n\n**Answer: (D) 36**"
      }
    ],
