    "prompt": "Mary was given the task of removing all multiples of 2 and 3 from the set of numbers from 1 to 100. The number of numbers that remained was",
    "image": null,
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "17"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "33"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "18"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "34"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "26"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "B",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Inclusion-exclusion",
        "body": "Multiples of 2: 50; of 3: 33; of 6: 16. Removed: $50+33-16=67$. Remaining: $100-67=33$.\n\n**Answer: (B) 33**"
      },
      {
        "title": "By blocks of 6",
        "body": "In each block of six consecutive numbers $6k+1,\\dots,6k+6$ only $6k+1$ and $6k+5$ survive. The numbers 1 to 96 give $16\\times2=32$, and from 97 to 100 only 97 survives (98 and 100 are even, 99 is a multiple of 3): $32+1=33$.\n\n**Answer: (B) 33**"
      }
    ],
