    "type": "mc",
    "prompt": "Three rulers and one pencil cost the same as two erasers. One ruler, two pencils and three erasers cost R25. If the price of each item is a whole number of Rands, then the price of an eraser is",
    "image": null,
    "choices": [
      {
        "key": "A",
        "text": "R2"
      },
      {
        "key": "B",
        "text": "R3"
      },
      {
        "key": "C",
        "text": "R4"
      },
      {
        "key": "D",
        "text": "R5"
      },
      {
        "key": "E",
        "text": "impossible to find"
      }
    ],
    "answer": "D",
    "acceptedAnswers": null,
    "answerUnit": null,
    "solutions": [
      {
        "title": "Equations",
        "body": "Let ruler $r$, pencil $p$, eraser $e$ (rand). $3r+p=2e$ and $r+2p+3e=25$. From the first, $p=2e-3r$; so $r+4e-6r+3e=25$, i.e. $7e-5r=25$ and $p=2e-3r>0$. Then $7e=25+5r$, so $r\\equiv2\\pmod 7$; $p>0$ forces $r\\le4$, so $r=2$, $e=5$, $p=4$. Check: $6+4=10=2\\times5$ and $2+8+15=25$.\n\n**Answer: (D) R5**"
      }
    ],
